WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.921
(audience cheering)

00:00:00.921 --> 00:00:02.880
- I know!

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.200
- Look at your pretty audience.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.160
- I, thank you!

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.607
- Your audience looks so pretty.

00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:07.440
- [Kelly] You look so beautiful.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.110
- You got lovely colors
on. Very springtime.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:10.980
- [Kelly] I know you do too.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.350
But I love the touch of rock
and roll with the leather.

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.760
This is my favorite part of it.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.384
- I'm always trying to be rock and roll.

00:00:16.384 --> 00:00:17.610
I'm failing.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.690
- [Kelly] No, you're not failing.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:19.650
You're always rock and roll.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.270
I literally was so
excited you were coming.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.920
I was in all caps, and my emails with

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.270
my Executive Producer this weekend.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.770
I was like, what?

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:26.603
I was very excited.

00:00:26.603 --> 00:00:27.990
Anyway, it's great to see you.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:28.980
Happy St. Patrick's Day.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.210
Do y'all celebrate that in London?

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.290
Did you grow up with that?

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.700
- You not so much as they do in New York.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.533
Funnily enough.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.366
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:35.370
- You know, I mean there's
a big Irish population

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.203
obviously in London.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:37.410
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.110
- But, New York is where
they really celebrate it.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:42.739
- [Kelly] Yeah, I think they
shut down streets and yeah.

00:00:42.739 --> 00:00:43.572
- [Helen] Yeah.

00:00:43.572 --> 00:00:45.000
That's, but it's in Ireland, it's honestly

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.980
it's more of a religious
holiday, you know,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.000
St. Patrick's Day.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:48.840
So it's not.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:49.860
- [Kelly] Yeah, so you know,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.653
they're doing it for the right reasons.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.190
- Don't get me wrong,
they celebrate. Yeah.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.350
- Would you like a
green beer to celebrate?

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.580
- I've never had a green beer.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.413
- [Kelly] Me neither! I don't think.

00:01:00.413 --> 00:01:02.340
Maybe I have on here, actually.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.420
I think that's the only other time.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.353
Yes. Let's do it.

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.260
Okay. This is Justin.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.093
- Justin.

00:01:08.093 --> 00:01:08.926
- Yes. This Justin.

00:01:08.926 --> 00:01:09.808
You get a fancy,

00:01:09.808 --> 00:01:10.641
- I'm not sure I want to
say thank you for that.

00:01:10.641 --> 00:01:12.240
- Worthy of a Dame, your cup.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.250
Look, I got the Average Joe cup.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.683
- How'd they make it green?

00:01:15.683 --> 00:01:17.220
- I'm, I'm sure.
- I guess they put dye in it.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.110
- [Kelly] Maybe it
involves giving us cancer.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.193
I'm not sure.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.605
Anyway, cheers! Green beer!
- Cheers, sweetie.

00:01:24.605 --> 00:01:27.770
- Take a tiny bit.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.603
Okay.

00:01:28.603 --> 00:01:29.880
- Wait a minute. Happy St. Patrick's Day.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.357
- Happy Saint Patty's Day, yeah.

00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:34.410
- Happy St. Patty's Day.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.940
- Yeah, just taste like beer.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:38.070
Yeah. Just your, yeah, beer, that's green.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.270
- You wouldn't even know
it was green, would you?

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.200
- Yeah, I know.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.280
You know what I just noticed,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.480
I don't even know if
you wanna talk about it,

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:44.100
but I have a tattoo right
here on me, as well.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.260
What, what does yours mean?

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.265
I just noticed it.

00:01:47.265 --> 00:01:48.098
- Are you kidding? You
got the same tattoo?

00:01:48.098 --> 00:01:50.010
- Not the same. I just noticed
it was in a similar place.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.420
- Oh, wasn't it painful?

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.000
- It, well, it, I was very inebriated.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.214
- Me too, me too.

00:01:56.214 --> 00:01:59.100
You'd have to be, really, don't you?

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.030
- What does it stand for?

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.590
- Mine was done with a safety pin, which,

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:02.610
so it took forever.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:03.443
- What?

00:02:03.443 --> 00:02:04.890
- [Helen] It was like a,
yeah, it was a Native American

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:05.790
who did it for me,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.150
and she was brilliant.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.916
She just put a little of
cotton around the end of the

00:02:10.916 --> 00:02:13.278
of the, you know, the pointy
bit of the safety pin,

00:02:13.278 --> 00:02:15.930
and they just stabbed my hand with it.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.390
It was so painful.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:21.000
Halfway through I said,
I can't stand it anymore.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.900
You stop.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.330
She said, no, once you've
committed to her tattoos

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.550
you held my hand, you've
gotta continue, you know.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:27.383
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:28.740
- She was absolutely right, of course.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.450
'Cuz half her tattoo
would've been terrible.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.590
- [Kelly] Would've been a little silly.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:32.423
- Yeah.

00:02:32.423 --> 00:02:33.960
- Did it mean anything special to you?

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.100
- It did actually.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.140
It, it kind of, it's two interlocking V's,

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.660
which means someone can
be as different from you

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.560
as you can possibly imagine,
but have equal value to you.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.390
And I thought that was
a very nice concept.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.070
- Wait, that's the kind
of tattoo you get drunk.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:50.471
What? That's not the
kinda tattoo I get when

00:02:50.471 --> 00:02:52.443
I'm inebriated. That was very prolific.

00:02:52.443 --> 00:02:53.441
I was like, wait, what?

00:02:53.441 --> 00:02:54.690
That's incredible.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.119
- My next one will be an anchor.

00:02:56.119 --> 00:02:56.952
- Okay.

00:03:00.077 --> 00:03:00.910
Okay.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.770
So wait, we just had the Oscars Sunday.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.840
So you, you didn't go, I know, I heard,

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.070
but like, did, did you watch it?

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:08.909
Did you, what was your favorite moment?

00:03:08.909 --> 00:03:10.170
- [Helen] I did watch
it, I was in a restaurant

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.190
actually watching it.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.410
They had it up on the thing,
so, so that was great to,

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.280
to watch that.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.140
- Anything that happen that you love?

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.103
- I cried when Brendan Fraser got,

00:03:18.103 --> 00:03:20.651
- [Kelly] Oh, it's so cool.
- Got the award. I cried.

00:03:20.651 --> 00:03:22.170
- [Kelly] He did such an incredible job.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.300
- [Helen] Yeah, I worked
with Brendan, you know

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.790
quite a few years ago on
a film called Inkheart.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.640
And he was, he is such a lovely person.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.408
He's the, I think you've
had him on your show.

00:03:31.408 --> 00:03:32.880
- Yeah, yeah. I've had
him on a couple times.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.800
- [Helen] And I'm sure you, you know how,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.600
what a beautiful man he is.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:39.390
He's a magical man, I think.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:41.520
And he was clearly very, very moved.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.740
It was a huge moment for him.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.500
So I, it was the right person for me.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.073
The, the way he responded to it, I, I,

00:03:48.073 --> 00:03:50.323
I just found it very moving,
is, it was the highlight

00:03:50.323 --> 00:03:52.260
for me of the whole show.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:54.030
- I love that when you're
rooting for someone

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.250
'cuz you really believe in
like, what their, either them

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.350
or their project, whatever
it may be, and then they win.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.910
That's a really good feeling
for everyone involved.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:00.810
- Yeah, it's great, it's great.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.960
- Yeah. What did it feel like
when you won for The Queen?

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.234
Were you, do you go into like,

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.402
do you remember, or do you just.

00:04:08.402 --> 00:04:10.650
- [Helen] I do remember. I do remember.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.483
You know, it, it's a

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:14.850
it, it is an incredible
moment in any actor's life.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:17.014
- [Kelly] Yeah, to be recognized.

00:04:17.014 --> 00:04:19.163
(audience clapping)

00:04:19.163 --> 00:04:21.990
- [Helen] You know, at
the same time, you know

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.997
it's not like an athletic race, you know.

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:27.930
Usain Bolt wins,

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:29.730
he is the fastest person.

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:30.630
- Oh.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:32.100
- [Helen] But you know what I'm saying?

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.780
In our world, it's not the same.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:34.623
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:34.623 --> 00:04:35.580
- You know, we are, we are not athletes.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:36.413
- [Kelly] It's subjective.

00:04:36.413 --> 00:04:38.040
- It's subjective and all the rest of it,

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.600
and luck, and all the rest of it.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.673
But, you know, when you get
to the Oscars, you've been

00:04:42.673 --> 00:04:46.110
you've been to a lot of
award shows by then, you know

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:48.990
obviously. So, you know, you've been

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:52.170
in this weird carousel of,

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.420
of self regard,

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.910
and talking about yourself endlessly.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:57.743
- Yes.

00:04:57.743 --> 00:05:00.420
- Sick about talking
yourself and, and, and,

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.340
and it's the final moment.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.394
So, it's a moment of,

00:05:04.394 --> 00:05:06.750
it's a weird moment
when in a way this sort

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:10.050
of beautiful bubble you've
been in, swirling around,

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.750
this bubble of award
shows is suddenly popped,

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.210
because that's the end of it.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.273
- Yeah.

00:05:16.273 --> 00:05:18.960
- So it's, it's, it's a
moment of incredible sort

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.540
of triumph, is not the
right word, but, you know

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.250
you feel incredible.

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:24.240
It's an incredible moment.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.070
I, I'm being very inarticulate.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:27.090
You can cut it all out.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.148
- [Kelly] No!

00:05:28.148 --> 00:05:28.981
I think it's,

00:05:28.981 --> 00:05:31.230
I, I am like anytime I,
I've never won anything

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:33.000
like an Oscar, but anytime I
want like a Grammy or anything

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.890
like that, my, sometimes I blank.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.328
I just blank 'cuz I don't
think I'm going to win.

00:05:37.328 --> 00:05:38.161
- Yes.

00:05:38.161 --> 00:05:38.994
- And then you win.
- And then you win.

00:05:38.994 --> 00:05:41.030
- Forget every human
I'm supposed to thank.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.507
Yeah. Oh, oh yeah.
- No, absolutely.

00:05:42.507 --> 00:05:44.552
- I'm just like screw
it. Thank all of you.

00:05:44.552 --> 00:05:45.880
- [Helen] Yeah, yeah no.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:46.713
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.057
- [Kelly] I just, I go kinda of foggy.

00:05:48.057 --> 00:05:49.257
- I'm not good with
those list of thank yous.

00:05:49.257 --> 00:05:51.303
You do go incredibly foggy.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:53.670
- That's so cool though.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.230
- It, it is an amazing moment.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:56.063
It is an absolute.

00:05:56.063 --> 00:05:58.200
And I remember thinking, well, this is it.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.100
This is the top.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.050
The only way now, is down.

00:06:01.924 --> 00:06:04.110
- But slides are fun! That's what I'd say.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:07.410
Your new movie is called
Shazam, Fury of the Gods.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:10.167
So, what was it like
playing a villain goddess?

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:12.150
- Well, first of all,
I'd seen the first one

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.770
and being completely charmed by it.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:14.603
I loved it.
- Me too.

00:06:14.603 --> 00:06:16.530
- So when they said, would
you like to be in Shazam?

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.390
I sort of thought, oh yeah, that, you know

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.710
I loved the first one, so why not?

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:21.660
And then the word goddess came up.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:22.660
- [Kelly] Hell yeah.

00:06:24.435 --> 00:06:25.685
Well of course.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.460
It's incredible, and I didn't know like,

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:30.750
you did some of your stunts, right?

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:31.590
Because.
- I did.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:33.780
- [Kelly] I'm hoping
you didn't do the scene

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.570
that you just get, yeah.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.520
Shazam takes you out, like a lot.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:39.450
- I did do that scene.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:40.680
- You did that scene?
- I did.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:42.180
I mean, not all of it.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.013
- Okay.

00:06:43.013 --> 00:06:43.846
- But I did a lot of it.

00:06:43.846 --> 00:06:44.840
- You get behind handed to you.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:45.753
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:47.543
But I hand it to him.

00:06:47.543 --> 00:06:48.720
- You do, you do.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:49.720
Try not to spoil it.

00:06:51.447 --> 00:06:53.760
She hands it to him as well.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.720
- I got my Shazam finger. This
is the result of my stunt.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:58.740
- [Kelly] Oh my God. Are are you kidding?

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.020
- You, can you see how bent that one?

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.430
This one's nice and straight.

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.500
That's my Shazam finger, yeah.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.300
- I feel like we have something in common.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.190
So I bent, I didn't
break it, but I bent it.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.440
So mine's bent too, my
other one to my, yeah.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:11.560
- This is a lot more
bent than your bent one.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:13.634
- [Kelly] Yeah, it does
look, it does look pretty,

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:15.191
who did that to you?

00:07:15.191 --> 00:07:16.620
- A concrete wall.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.180
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.204
- A concrete wall.

00:07:19.204 --> 00:07:20.200
- Oh my God.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.320
So that didn't go over well.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:23.340
- In, in the fight.

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:25.353
I was hoping to hit Zach.

00:07:25.353 --> 00:07:27.690
And, and the stunt guy
said, you must follow

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.730
through, 'cuz otherwise
it doesn't look good.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:31.170
So I went, okay, I'll follow through.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.820
You know, bam!

00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.950
Right into the concrete wall.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:38.520
So, but I was very stunty,
you know, which is yeah,

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.350
no it's fine. It's
fine. No, no, it's fine.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:41.183
No carry on.

00:07:41.183 --> 00:07:42.503
- It's like killing you
and you're like, I'm great!

00:07:42.503 --> 00:07:44.053
- No, no, I'm great. I'm great.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.530
- Oh, I would've been a baby about it.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:47.363
Somebody help me.

00:07:47.363 --> 00:07:49.530
Like I would've been
a total baby about it.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.363
I love it though.

00:07:50.363 --> 00:07:52.517
I didn't know the whole story behind,

00:07:52.517 --> 00:07:54.570
we had Zachary here, and I
didn't know the whole story

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.610
behind, even how Shazam his name.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:57.990
Like, I didn't, I didn't realize

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.310
like how the gods fit
into it and everything.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.143
And I thought that was really cool.

00:08:00.143 --> 00:08:01.020
Cause I love mythology.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:02.520
- It was a great idea.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:03.993
- Because they were the Superman.

00:08:03.993 --> 00:08:06.630
They were the superheroes
of 2000 years ago.

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:07.463
- Yeah.

00:08:07.463 --> 00:08:08.370
- [Helen] That was why people told stories

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:09.203
about them, you know?

00:08:09.203 --> 00:08:10.036
- Yeah.

